.\" Manpage for kanban (Open Kanban CLI)
.\" Hand-written; the canonical reference lives in
.\" docs/CLI_COMMANDS.md and cli/README.md.
.TH KANBAN 1 "2026-09-12" "0.1.0" "Open Kanban CLI"

.SH NAME
kanban \- command\-line client for the Open Kanban board

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kanban
[\fI\-\-api\-url\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fI\-\-profile\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fI\-\-output\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
[\fI\-\-color\fR|\fI\-\-no\-color\fR]
[\fI\-h\fR|\fI\-\-help\fR]
[\fI\-V\fR|\fI\-\-version\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kanban
is the official command\-line client for the Open Kanban
(https://github.com/songkl/open-kanban) task board. It authenticates
against the Kanban server using OAuth 2.1 (RFC 7591 dynamic client
registration + RFC 8628 device authorization grant), then drives every
read/write surface exposed by the HTTP API.

The CLI is a thin wrapper over the same JSON API used by the React web UI
and the
.B open\-kanban\-mcp
server. The full flag\-level reference for every command lives in
\fIdocs/CLI_COMMANDS.md\fR; onboarding, configuration, exit codes and
troubleshooting live in \fIcli/README.md\fR.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the CLI version and exit.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the root help text (command tree) and exit. Pass a command path
(\fBkanban help tasks create\fR) for per\-command help.

.TP
.BR \-\-api\-url " " \fIURL\fR
Kanban API base URL. Overrides
.B KANBAN_API_URL
and the value stored in
\fI~/.config/kanban\-cli/config.json\fR.
Default:
.BR http://localhost:8080 .

.TP
.BR \-\-profile " " \fINAME\fR
Credential profile name. Use distinct profiles to keep multiple accounts
(e.g.\&\fBwork\fR and \fBpersonal\fR) side\-by\-side without overwriting
each other. Overrides
.BR KANBAN_CLI_PROFILE .

.TP
.BR \-\-output " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output renderer: \fBtable\fR (default, ANSI when stdout is a TTY) or
\fBjson\fR. The flag also accepts \fByaml\fR but currently renders as
\fBtable\fR; pipe \fB\-\-output json\fR through
.BR yq (1)
or
.BR jq (1)
in the meantime.

.TP
.BR \-\-color " " \fIMODE\fR
Force ANSI color: \fBon\fR, \fBoff\fR, or \fBauto\fR (default;
honours \fBNO_COLOR\fR / \fB FORCE_COLOR\fR / TTY detection).

.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color in table output. Equivalent to
.BR \-\-color=off .

.SH COMMANDS

.SS Authentication
.TP
.B kanban auth login
Start the OAuth 2.1 device authorization grant, print the verification
URL + user code to stderr, and persist the issued tokens at
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kanban\-cli/credentials\-\fI<api>\fI.json\fR
(mode \fB0600\fR).

.TP
.B kanban auth status
Print the active profile, host, scope and access\-token lifetime.

.TP
.B kanban auth logout
Delete the stored credentials (idempotent).

.TP
.B kanban auth whoami [\fB\-\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR]
Call \fBGET\fR \fIPATH\fR (default
.BR /api/v1/users/me )
and print the resolved user.

.SS Read\-only
.TP
.B kanban status
Probe the Kanban API; print latency, boards count, and a per\-board list.
Public endpoint \-\- does not require authentication.

.TP
.B kanban dashboard
Fetch \fBGET /api/v1/dashboard/stats\fR and print totals plus per\-status
and per\-priority breakdowns. Auth required.

.TP
.B kanban boards list
[\fB\-\-fields\fR \fIFIELDS\fR]
List non\-deleted boards (\fBGET /api/v1/boards\fR). Public.

.TP
.B kanban boards get \fIID\fR
[\fB\-\-fields\fR \fIFIELDS\fR]
Fetch a single board (\fBGET /api/v1/boards/:id\fR). Public.

.TP
.B kanban columns list
[\fB\-\-board\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-positions\fR \fIPOS\fR]
[\fB\-\-fields\fR \fIFIELDS\fR]
List columns (\fBGET /api/v1/columns\fR), optionally filtered.
Public.

.TP
.B kanban columns get \fIID\fR
[\fB\-\-fields\fR \fIFIELDS\fR]
Fetch a single column (\fBGET /api/v1/columns/:id\fR). Public.

.TP
.B kanban tasks list
[\fB\-\-board\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-column\fR|\fB\-\-status\fR \fIVAL\fR]
[\fB\-\-agent\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR]
[\fB\-\-priority\fR \fIP\fR]
[\fB\-\-assignee\fR \fIUSER\fR]
[\fB\-\-search\fR \fIQ\fR]
[\fB\-\-since\fR \fItoday|thisWeek|thisMonth\fR]
[\fB\-\-tag\fR \fITAG\fR]
[\fB\-\-lightweight\fR]
[\fB\-\-fields\fR \fIid|id+updated\fR]
List tasks (filters applied client\-side over
.BR /api/v1/columns ).
\fB\-\-column\fR and \fB\-\-status\fR are mutually exclusive.

.TP
.B kanban tasks get \fIID\fR
Fetch a single task (\fBGET /api/v1/tasks/:id\fR). Public.

.SS Tasks (auth required)
.TP
.B kanban tasks create
\fB\-\-title\fR \fITITLE\fR
[\fB\-\-description\fR \fIDESC\fR]
[\fB\-\-column\fR|\fB\-\-status\fR \fIVAL\fR]
[\fB\-\-board\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-priority\fR \fIP\fR]
[\fB\-\-assignee\fR \fIUSER\fR]
[\fB\-\-meta\fR \fIKEY=VAL\fR...]
[\fB\-\-no\-publish\fR]
Create a task (\fBPOST /api/v1/tasks\fR).
\fB\-\-column\fR and \fB\-\-status\fR are mutually exclusive; the CLI
resolves \fB\-\-status\fR to a column by Chinese name within
\fB\-\-board\fR (or any board).

.TP
.B kanban tasks update \fIID\fR
[\fB\-\-title\fR \fIT\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR \fID\fR]
[\fB\-\-priority\fR \fIP\fR] [\fB\-\-assignee\fR \fIU\fR]
[\fB\-\-meta\fR \fIK=V\fR...]
[\fB\-\-column\fR|\fB\-\-status\fR \fIVAL\fR]
Update a task (\fBPUT /api/v1/tasks/:id\fR).
At least one patch flag is required.

.TP
.B kanban tasks delete \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Delete a task (\fBDELETE /api/v1/tasks/:id\fR). Confirmation is
always skipped in current handlers.

.TP
.B kanban tasks complete \fIID\fR
Advance a task to the next column
(\fBPOST /api/v1/tasks/:id/complete\fR).

.TP
.B kanban tasks move \fIID\fR
\fB\-\-column\fR|\fB\-\-status\fR \fIVAL\fR
Move a task to a target column or status. Exactly one of
\fB\-\-column\fR / \fB\-\-status\fR is required.

.SS Batch tasks (auth required)
.TP
.B kanban tasks batch create
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-title\fR \fIT\fR...]
[\fB\-\-description\fR \fID\fR...]
[\fB\-\-column\fR \fIC\fR...]
[\fB\-\-status\fR \fIS\fR...]
[\fB\-\-priority\fR \fIP\fR...]
[\fB\-\-assignee\fR \fIU\fR...]
[\fB\-\-published\fR \fIB\fR...]
Create multiple tasks (\fBPOST /api/v1/tasks/batch\fR). Either
\fB\-\-file\fR (JSON or YAML) or repeated flags aligned positionally.

.TP
.B kanban tasks batch update \fIIDS\fR...
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-column\fR|\fB\-\-status\fR \fIVAL\fR]
[\fB\-\-priority\fR \fIP\fR]
[\fB\-\-assignee\fR \fIU\fR]
Update many tasks at once (\fBPUT /api/v1/tasks/batch\fR).

.TP
.B kanban tasks batch delete \fIIDS\fR...
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Delete many tasks at once (\fBDELETE /api/v1/tasks/batch\fR).

.SS Drafts and archive (auth required)
.TP
.B kanban drafts list [\fB\-\-board\fR \fIID\fR]
.TP
.B kanban drafts publish \fIID\fR
.TP
.B kanban drafts unpublish \fIID\fR
.TP
.B kanban archived list [\fB\-\-board\fR \fIID\fR]
.TP
.B kanban archived archive \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.TP
.B kanban archived restore \fIID\fR

.SS Comments (auth required)
.TP
.B kanban comments add \fITASK\fR \fB\-\-body\fR \fITEXT\fR
[\fB\-\-author\fR \fINAME\fR]
Add a comment. Pass \fB\-\-body\ \-\fR to read the body from stdin
(UTF\-8, trimmed; internal newlines preserved).

.TP
.B kanban comments list \fITASK\fR
List comments for a task.

.SS Subtasks (auth required)
.TP
.B kanban subtasks list \fITASK\fR
.TP
.B kanban subtasks create \fITASK\fR \fB\-\-title\fR \fIT\fR
.TP
.B kanban subtasks update \fIID\fR
[\fB\-\-title\fR \fIT\fR]
[\fB\-\-completed\fR|\fB\-\-no\-completed\fR]
At least one of \fB\-\-title\fR / \fB\-\-completed\fR is required.
.TP
.B kanban subtasks delete \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR]

.SS Mine and workspace (auth required)
.TP
.B kanban mine [\fB\-\-board\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-lightweight\fR]
List tasks assigned to (or routed to) the current agent. The
\fB\-\-board\fR flag is currently a no\-op (the endpoint does not accept
it); a warning is written to stderr.

.TP
.B kanban workspace upload \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-path\fR \fIREMOTE\fR]
.TP
.B kanban workspace batch\-upload \fIFILES\fR...
.TP
.B kanban workspace list [\fB\-\-path\fR \fISUB\fR]
.TP
.B kanban workspace read \fIID\fR
.TP
.B kanban workspace delete \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.TP
.B kanban workspace stats

.SS Interactive REPL
.TP
.B kanban shell
Start an interactive REPL with the prompt \fBkanban>\fR. Built\-in
commands: \fBhelp\fR, \fBexit\fR/\fBquit\fR, \fBclear\fR, \fBwhoami\fR.
Anything else is dispatched to a fresh \fBparseAsync\fR; history is
persisted to \fI~/.kanban_shell_history\fR
(override via \fBKANBAN_SHELL_HISTORY\fR).

.SS Runner loop
.TP
.B kanban run [\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[{\fB\-\-board\fR \fIID\fR \fB\-\-status\fR \fIS\fR | \fB\-\-mine\fR}]
[\fB\-\-once\fR]
Start the long\-lived runner loop that watches a board/column (mode-1)
or the authenticated agent's task inbox (mode-2), spawns the agent
binary, heartbeats every \fBheartbeatIntervalMs\fR, and reports the
outcome back via \fBPOST /api/v1/runs/:taskId/finish\fR. SIGINT /
SIGTERM trigger a graceful drain. See
\fIcli/man/kanban-run.1.md\fR for the full reference and
\fIdevDoc/CLI_RUNNER_PLAN_2026-09-12.md\fR for the design plan.

.SS Shell completion
.TP
.B kanban completion bash | zsh | fish
Emit a self\-contained completion script to stdout. Install hints are
printed to stderr. See \fIcli/README.md\fR for the install snippets.

.SS Configuration
.TP
.B kanban config get [\fIKEY\fR]
Print the resolved value of \fIKEY\fR (one of \fBapiUrl\fR, \fBoutput\fR,
\fBprofile\fR, \fBtimeout\fR) alongside its source (\fBcli\fR /
\fBenv\fR / \fBfile\fR / \fBdefault\fR). With no key, prints every
supported key.

.TP
.B kanban config set \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Persist \fIKEY\fR=\fIVALUE\fR to
\fI~/.config/kanban\-cli/config.json\fR (mode \fB0600\fR). Unknown keys
or invalid values raise an error and exit \fB1\fR.

.SH EXIT STATUS
The CLI uses stable POSIX\-style exit codes so scripts can branch
without parsing stderr:
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid usage (missing / conflicting flags) or other unexpected error.
.TP
.B 2
Not logged in (run \fBkanban auth login\fR first).
.TP
.B 3
User denied / device code expired during login, or HTTP 404
(\fBNotFoundError\fR).
.TP
.B 4
Server error (HTTP 5xx).
.TP
.B 5
Resource not found (e.g.\&board / task / column id missing).
.TP
.B 6
Network error (server unreachable, DNS failure, TLS error, ...).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kanban\-cli/config.json
Persistent CLI configuration. Mode \fB0600\fR on write. Honours
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kanban\-cli/credentials\-\fI<api>\fI.json
OAuth 2.1 tokens issued by the Kanban server. Mode \fB0600\fR on
write. One file per API URL.
.TP
.I ~/.kanban_shell_history
REPL command history (override via \fBKANBAN_SHELL_HISTORY\fR).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KANBAN_API_URL
Default value for \fBapiUrl\fR (overridden by the flag and by the
config file).
.TP
.B KANBAN_CLI_PROFILE
Default value for \fBprofile\fR.
.TP
.B KANBAN_CLI_OUTPUT
Default value for \fBoutput\fR.
.TP
.B KANBAN_CLI_TIMEOUT
HTTP timeout in milliseconds (config and env only \-\- not a CLI flag).
.TP
.B KANBAN_SHELL_HISTORY
Override the path to the REPL history file.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI color when \fB\-\-color=auto\fR (the default) is in effect.
.TP
.B FORCE_COLOR
Force ANSI color when \fB\-\-color=auto\fR is in effect.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Override the base directory for the CLI config and credentials files
(default \fB~/.config\fR).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "Log in and probe the API:"
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ export KANBAN_API_URL=https://kanban.example.com
$ kanban auth login
$ kanban status
.RE
.fi

.TP
.B "Create a task and drive it across the board:"
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ kanban tasks create \-\-title "Ship docs" \-\-priority high
$ kanban tasks move  t\-123 \-\-status in_progress
$ kanban tasks complete t\-123
.RE
.fi

.TP
.B "Pipe a multi\-line review into a comment:"
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ echo "Reviewed the OAuth flow.\enLooks good." \\
    | kanban comments add t\-123 \-\-body \-
.RE
.fi

.TP
.B "Bulk\-update from a YAML file:"
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ kanban tasks batch create \-\-file ./tasks.yaml
.RE
.fi

.TP
.B "Resolve which API URL the CLI is talking to:"
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ kanban config get apiUrl
http://localhost:8080 (default)
.RE
.fi

